// Ported verbatim (CSS classes/ids preserved) from the artifact's Mapfre
// card illustration (project/Main.dc.html, card index 0 -- "Driving 35%
// YoY growth"). This is the tile-mosaic that reshuffles on hover/focus via
// the `.mp-t0`..`.mp-t19` transition-delayed transforms and `.mp-w0`..`.mp-w6`
// word wipes defined in home.css -- all pure CSS, no JS needed for the
// hover interaction itself. The two embedded base64 raster images were
// extracted to /public/cards/mapfre-texture.jpg and mapfre-strip.png rather
// than kept inline, since embedding ~100KB of base64 directly in a JS
// bundle is wasteful -- the <image> href attributes below now point at
// those real files.
//
// Rendered via dangerouslySetInnerHTML rather than hand-converted JSX: the
// source SVG is ~130KB of generated path data with hundreds of attributes
// (clip-path, mask-type, etc.) that would need camelCasing one by one for
// JSX, with no reliable way to verify a transcription error in a file this
// size. The raw markup below is exactly what shipped in the artifact
// (post base64-extraction), so correctness here rests on the extraction
// step, not on manual attribute-by-attribute conversion.

