// This card takes no props and has no JS logic at all -- it relies purely
// on the `.is-current`/`:hover` CSS transition in home-mobile.css/home.css,
// exactly like Phantom/Pulso/victorai do, on both desktop and mobile.
//
// History of this card's Safari/iPhone bug (Victoria reported the tile
// mosaic never animating on her phone, repeatedly, across three different
// fix attempts):
// - Fix #14: added `will-change` to the `.mp-tile`/`.mp-word` elements.
//   Didn't help -- confirmed by Victoria.
// - Fix #15: added an `active` prop + a `useEffect` that toggled the `<g
//   mask="...">` element's `mask` attribute off and back on every time the
//   card centred/un-centred, meant to force Safari to recompute a mask
//   bitmap suspected of going stale. Never confirmed fixed on a real
//   iPhone, and Victoria then reported something worse and more specific:
//   the card flickered once when centred, then the mosaic never animated
//   at all -- consistent with the attribute toggle itself interrupting the
//   tiles'/words' own in-flight CSS transition rather than fixing
//   anything.
// - Fix #17d reverted fix #15's hack back to plain CSS (no JS at all,
//   `active` prop removed). Chromium here never reproduced any of this
//   (desktop, which never ran the hack, always animated fine too), so this
//   could only be confirmed as "doesn't regress anything," not as "fixes
//   the bug" -- and Victoria confirmed it was STILL broken on her device.
// - Fix #18 (this version): rather than trying a fourth variant of
//   poking the mask from JS, the SVG was changed to not use an SVG
//   `<mask>` at all. The `.mp-tile` rects here were always simple,
//   solid-fill shapes (no partial opacity/color blending) used only to
//   carve a binary visible/hidden window into the pattern-image rect
//   below them -- exactly what an SVG `<clipPath>` does too, through a
//   completely different rendering pipeline that doesn't share the
//   `<mask>`-bitmap-goes-stale class of WebKit bugs fix #15 was chasing.
//   `<mask id="m">`/`mask="url(#m)"` became `<clipPath id="m">`/
//   `clip-path="url(#m)"`, with no other change to the tile geometry,
//   CSS, or transitions -- the mosaic should look and animate identically
//   everywhere this bug was never seen (this environment, desktop), and
//   this sidesteps the suspected cause everywhere it might still exist.
//   Still not verified on an actual iPhone. If this ALSO doesn't resolve
//   it, the bug isn't about `<mask>` specifically (already ruled out by
//   this fix) -- next suspect the `<g clip-path="...">`'s own ancestor
//   `<g clip-path="url(#clip0_80_51)">` wrapper, or abandon SVG clipping
//   for this card entirely and compute the tile window in JS/React,
//   setting each tile's visible region via individual positioned
//   <image>/<rect> elements instead of a shared clip region.
//
// Fix #39 (2026-10-28): removed that exact next suspect -- the outer
// `<g clip-path="url(#clip0_80_51)">` wrapper around this card's entire
// SVG content (tiles, word-wipe paths, everything). Its own `<clipPath
// id="clip0_80_51">` definition was a plain `<rect width="300"
// height="400" fill="white"/>` -- unrounded, exactly matching this SVG's
// own `viewBox="0 0 300 400"`. That makes it a pure no-op: the SVG's
// `viewBox` plus a root `<svg>`'s implicit `overflow:hidden` (per spec)
// already constrain rendering to those identical bounds, so removing this
// redundant clip-path ancestor has zero visual effect here or anywhere.
// But it WAS an ancestor sitting between the `.mp-tile`/`.mp-word`
// elements and the SVG root -- exactly the shape of the WebKit bug class
// already on record in this file (fix #18b, above) and in
// home-mobile.css's fix #14 comment: content clipped by an ancestor fails
// to repaint when a descendant's `transform` changes via a one-shot CSS
// `transition` (vs. a looping `animation`, which forces a repaint every
// frame regardless and so never hits this bug). Mapfre's tile-mosaic/
// word-wipe is the only one of the six cards driven by a one-shot
// `transition` rather than a looping `animation` -- consistent with it
// being the only card with this reported bug.
// Still UNVERIFIED on a real iPhone -- same caveat as every prior Mapfre
// attempt (fixes #14/#15/#17d/#18b): this environment only has Chromium,
// which has never reproduced the bug either. If this ALSO doesn't resolve
// it, this removal plus the `will-change` workaround already in
// home-mobile.css exhaust the "fix via CSS/structure alone" options for
// this card, and the next escalation is converting Mapfre's animation
// trigger from a one-shot CSS `transition` to a JS-driven
// `activate()`/`deactivate()` pattern matching AXACard.js/UndpCard.js
// (neither of which has this reported bug) -- strategy (b) from the
// investigation that led to this fix.
//
// Fix #27 (2026-10-28): every id this SVG defines, all private to this
// card's own clipping/texturing (none referenced from outside -- see
// lib/svgNamespace.js's header comment for why that matters). HomeMobile.js
// now mounts TWO instances of this exact card at once (the real slot plus
// its fix-#25 clone, see that file), and without a per-instance suffix on
// these the two instances' identical `id="clip0_80_51"` etc. collide --
// confirmed live as the cause of Victoria's "next card renders solid
// black" report when the carousel wraps onto this card's cloned slot.
const MAPFRE_IDS = ['clip1_80_51', 'image0_80_51', 'image1_80_51', 'pattern0_80_51', 'pattern1_80_51', 'm'];

function MapfreCard({ uid = '' } = {}) {
  const wrapRef = useRef(null);
  // Only actually rewrites anything when `uid` is non-empty -- HomeDesktop.js
  // never passes one (it only ever mounts a single instance), so desktop's
  // output is byte-identical to before this fix.
  const svg = useMemo(() => namespaceSvgIds(MAPFRE_SVG, MAPFRE_IDS, uid), [uid]);

  return <div ref={wrapRef} className="mp-card-wrap" dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: svg }} />;
}

// Memoized: `uid` (fix #27) is the only prop, and it's stable for the
// lifetime of a given mounted slot (HomeMobile.js passes the strip
// position, which never changes for an already-mounted instance), so this
// still never re-renders in practice once mounted, even though it's
// re-mounted inside the mobile/desktop carousel whose parent re-renders on
// every `setPos()`/scroll tick (see HomeMobile.js/HomeDesktop.js). Without
// memo, React would re-run and re-diff this ~100KB inline SVG tree on every
// one of those renders -- six (now eight, fix #25) times over -- which is
// the main cause of the janky/slow drag feel reported on mobile. memo()
// skips all of that entirely here, same reasoning as AXACard.js/
// UndpCard.js (which still take `active` and so still re-render when it
// changes).
export default memo(MapfreCard);
